menu "Linux Bridge Exporter (Power Base -> Linux OTBR host)"

    config LINUX_BRIDGE_EXPORTER_QUEUE_LEN
        int "Bounded export event queue depth"
        default 32
        help
            Depth of the queue between power_base_transport's bridge-observer
            callbacks (OT-task context, non-blocking enqueue only) and this
            component's own sending task. A full queue drops the newest event
            with a rate-limited warning rather than blocking the OT task or
            halting anything -- see components/linux_bridge_exporter's own
            header comment. The periodic full topology resync below recovers
            any dropped TOPOLOGY event; a dropped SAMPLE event is simply not
            exported (the power base's own aggregator still has it).

    config LINUX_BRIDGE_EXPORTER_FULL_RESYNC_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Full topology resync interval (ms)"
        default 5000
        help
            Every this many ms, resend every topology_registry node's
            CURRENT state to the Linux host, regardless of whether anything
            changed -- recovers from a dropped event, a stale/rebuilt Linux
            registry, or a Linux OTBR host that just restarted (this
            follow-up's own explicit requirement).

    config LINUX_BRIDGE_EXPORTER_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Bridge exporter heartbeat interval (ms)"
        default 10000
        help
            Liveness-only signal (power_base_uuid + uptime_ms + node_count);
            never authoritative -- the periodic full topology resync above is
            what actually reconciles Linux-side state.

endmenu
